{# Physical Letters: an NPC may write to the player unprompted.  Sent by the plugin with
   PublicSendCustomPromptToLLM; context variables:
     npc              UUID, name of the NPC who might write
     recipient        the player's name
     days_since_seen  game days since the NPC last dealt with the player (-1 unknown)
     correspondence   earlier letters between the two that the NPC knows of, oldest first
                      (up to 20): from, to, days_ago, body
     memories         the NPC's memories most relevant to the player (letters excluded) #}

{# How many of the most recent earlier letters to show. #}
{% set max_earlier_letters = 5 %}

{% set actor = decnpc(npc.UUID) %}
{% set first_earlier_letter = length(correspondence) - max_earlier_letters %}
[ system ]
    You are helping decide whether {{ actor.name }} writes a letter to {{ recipient }} today, unprompted, and if so, what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} writes. Stay true to {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} personality, background, speech patterns and relationship with {{ recipient }}.

    {{ render_character_profile("full", npc.UUID) }}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    {% if days_since_seen >= 0 %}
    ## Time Apart
    {% if days_since_seen == 0 %}{{ actor.name }} dealt with {{ recipient }} earlier today.{% else if days_since_seen == 1 %}{{ actor.name }} last dealt with {{ recipient }} a day ago.{% else %}{{ actor.name }} last dealt with {{ recipient }} {{ days_since_seen }} days ago.{% endif %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if correspondence and length(correspondence) > 0 %}
    ## Earlier Letters Between {{ actor.name }} and {{ recipient }}
    {% for earlier in correspondence %}
    {% if loop.index >= first_earlier_letter %}
    From {{ earlier.from }} to {{ earlier.to }}, {% if earlier.days_ago == 0 %}earlier today{% else if earlier.days_ago == 1 %}a day ago{% else %}{{ earlier.days_ago }} days ago{% endif %}:
    ```
    {{ earlier.body }}
    ```
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if memories and length(memories) > 0 %}
    ## What {{ actor.name }} Remembers of {{ recipient }}
    {% for memory in memories -%}
    - {{ memory }}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    ## Instructions

    1. **Decide whether {{ actor.name }} writes.** People write when they have a reason: news of their own, something unfinished between them, gratitude, worry, a favour to ask, a grudge, or simply missing someone. Someone who barely knows {{ recipient }}, or has nothing to say, doesn't write. It's fine to decide not to.

    2. **If {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} writes, write the letter** in {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} own voice: addressed to {{ recipient }}, a few short paragraphs at most, signed with {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} name. Draw on what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} remembers and on {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} own life as the profile describes it. {{ actor.name }} can only write about what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} knows; don't invent major events. If there are earlier letters, this continues a correspondence: stay consistent and don't repeat what was already written.

    3. **Write the memory {{ actor.name }} keeps of writing it**, in first person as {{ actor.name }}, one or two sentences: that {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} wrote to {{ recipient }} and what about.

    **IMPORTANT**: Return ONLY a valid JSON object. Do not include explanatory text before or after the JSON.

    Return JSON with exactly these fields:
    - 'write': true if {{ actor.name }} writes, false if not
    - 'letter': the letter, or "" if {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} doesn't write
    - 'memory': the first-person memory described above, or "" if {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} doesn't write
    - 'emotion': {{ actor.name }}'s main feeling while writing, one word (e.g. "fond", "worried", "restless")
    - 'importance': how much the letter matters to {{ actor.name }} (0.0-1.0 float)
[ end user ]
